    10	
    11	**No finding is WRONG in the sense of this file: the prototype shows no model claim or checked property to
    12	be false.** The evidence:
    13	
    14	- **Positive evidence.** Both symbolic attack traces replay with real Ed25519 signatures. The verifier
    15	  built from spec §5 rejects them on the checks the model names: C-C2 on V17/V18, C-C5 on V19 alone. The
    16	  mutants that remove exactly those checks accept (PHASE1-REPORT l.13-20, l.92-98). The registered
    17	  degraded cost (case (d), `AcceptS ⟹ IssuerSigned` red, CAP l.91) shows up concretely as d2 = d3
    18	  (PHASE2 l.149-157). S-P7's model also accepts an outer layer independently of its inner check
    19	  (`AcceptOuter` precedes `InnerCheck`, `s-p7/proverif/sp7_q2_degraded_compromised.pv:328-333`), which
    20	  matches the prototype's `VALID_DEGRADED` outer layer beside an `INVALID` inner one.
    21	- **The one result that looks like a violation is the prototype's own.** In case (e) a key revoked
    22	  inside (declared, anchor] verified `VALID_STRICT`, which contradicts P6. The cause is
    23	  `tessera_proto/verifier.py:315-317`, which maps "no revocation entry" to `PASS`. That is a misreport
    24	  under R-5.33 (spec l.1384), not a counterexample to P6 (see §6).
    25	- **What the prototype finds instead is 21 MISSING items.** In each, a model claim holds only under a
    26	  condition that neither the model nor the spec states, or the design needs a fact that no model
    27	  carries. Six bear on the capstone (§3). The deepest are:
    28	  - G-17: the required binding-form set;
    29	  - G-21: authority-channel scope;
    30	  - G-27: revocation has no carrier.
    31	- **How strong the "none WRONG" evidence is depends on the area.**
    32	  - Where the prototype stubbed *exactly as the model abstracts*, it could not have found a WRONG: the
    33	    authority channels are one Ed25519 key each (G-21), the anchor is a hash chain (G-20), and KMS and
    34	    GPG are both Ed25519 (G-12, G-13).
    35	  - The G-21 and P1-1 entries below are places where a real primitive *could* contradict a model claim.
