    48	Each of these is defensible, but the author would defend most of them by reading the AI's reasoning. That is the
    49	failure H2 names.
    50	
    51	**The author's own reading**, 2026-10-13:
    52	> *"I've been actively involved, but realistically I have not made every critical decision. I'd argue that's the
    53	> right balance."*
    54	>
    55	> *"I suppose, at some level, it _is_ 'vibe coded'. I explained (often multiple times) my goals for the project and
    56	> AI have run with that, lost themselves in the details, forgotten the higher objectives, re-learned of them from
    57	> where I asked questions or made suggestions that the direction was drifting, but in the end AI has been
    58	> implementing things."*
    59	
    60	He also drew a distinction the provenance labels miss: *"if something is presented to me and I agree with it, that
    61	is 'did not object' but it doesn't mean I did not consider the option, either."*
    62	
    63	## 3. The outcome — OWNER reading, contestable
    64	
    65	**H2 as registered is falsified.**
    66	- Load-bearing decisions exist that the author did not make.
    67	- He would justify them from the AI's reasoning.
    68	- The schedule assumption also failed.
    69	
    70	**What survives is narrower, and still checkable.** The author steered by goals and by tests of drift, not by
    71	ruling on detail. The process lost the higher objective repeatedly and recovered it each time, through his
    72	questions and through external lenses:
    73	- the prototype exposed what the model was missing (`prototype/TRIAGE.md`: 0 WRONG, 21 MISSING);
    74	- the 4 December test hands a non-expert only the documentation and the tools, and asks them to verify receipts
    75	  with Tessera switched off.
    76	
    77	The difference between this and "vibe coding" is real only if those external checks are what catch the drift.
    78	That makes 4 December the evidence for the narrower claim as well as for the product. If the tester accepts an
    79	unsafe receipt, both fail.
    80	
    81	**This is a result, not a reason to stop.** Prereg line 734: not proceeding as designed *"is a valid, honest
    82	outcome of this pre-registration, not a failure to conceal."* The project continues to the 4 December ship-or-stop
    83	gate (accepted 2026-10-09).
    84	
    85	## 4. Going forward
    86	
    87	- **Recording consideration.** When the author has considered an owner recommendation and agrees, one sentence of
    88	  his reason turns "did not object" into **AUTHOR ADOPTED**. That costs him a sentence, not a review, so it is not
    89	  theater. Without the sentence, the label stays OWNER.
    90	- **Not routed to the author.** Prover output, vector tables and review findings. The owner reads these; the
    91	  author gets the conclusions and the decisions that change direction.
    92	- **Proposed README credibility line** (for the author to adopt, edit or refuse):
    93	  > AI here contributes mechanics, rigor, adversarial review, and — since September 2026, by explicit delegation —
    94	  > ownership of the detailed design. The author sets direction, asks the questions that catch drift, and builds
    95	  > the external tests that would expose it. The original line ("AI … never contributes ownership") was registered
    96	  > as H2 and is recorded as falsified in `docs/h2-record-2026-10-13.md`. Whether stewardship by direction and
    97	  > external test is enough is what the 4 December relying-party test decides.

